& [Problem]
  + SWA-06B2B1 physically persisted a supplied successor on a disposable fixture but deliberately stopped before boot validation or recovery
  + a failed candidate therefore needed a recovery-owned deterministic restoration path that preserved evidence and never converted a supplied failure trigger into live activation authority

& [Solution]
  + one safe cantor_ecosystem kernel fully replays the exact B2B1 receipt marker commission root and failed registry before physical mutation
  + it reacquires bounded raw predecessor and failed-candidate bytes preserves the candidate constructs a distinct generation-plus-one restored record and reuses the ordered same-parent create-new write flush reopen replace parent-flush final-reopen protocol
  + the strict receipt records all physical observations while keeping boot validation live activation provider model process network and cleanup false
  + typed failures retain physical_contact replacement_performed owned_temp_removed and failed_candidate_preserved so partial effects cannot masquerade as atomic refusal success or completed recovery

& [Evidence]
  + the exact corrected upstream fixture is 49484 bytes SHA256 018D955E43C13EF8CC294F3271326824443DEB56F8C5FD00730ABB05A1B85E1E and binds distinct 93-byte failed and predecessor sources
  + focused WSL verification passes B2A 45 combined 16 and standalone rollback 9 in both debug and overflow-checked release
  + exact locked offline serialized workspace debug and overflow-checked release each pass 206 groups 1307 tests zero failed three ignored
  + an independent provider-free verifier rehashes the controlled artifact graph and adversarially refuses evidence laundering

& [Boundary]
